`, `CROSS_FAMILY_BYPASS`, `ACCEPTED_PENDING_REVIEW`, `--test-simulated*`, or `controller.simulate` reachable from `runtime/run_curriculum.py` or `runtime/langgraph_factory/*.py`.\n- `load_job_registry` (`transport.py:152`) hard-fails unless the job registry declares exactly 8 jobs and has exactly 8 entries.\n\nFull commands and output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/production_path_audit.txt`.\n\n## 4. Eight-job / authority / denominator / repair / persistence / resume / terminal / CLI invariants (TEST item 4)\n\nAll 7 classes re-verified directly from source (file:line evidence), not\nfrom result-markdown prose. Full report:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/invariant_audit.txt`. Summary:\n\n1. Eight model jobs, enforced by `load_job_registry` — **PASS**\n2. Authority: `FORBIDDEN_MODEL_FIELDS` rejects any model schema/candidate proposing control fields — **PASS**\n3. Denominators: `compute_unit_denominator` recomputes fresh per call; `classify_join_members` rejects extra/stale/cross-unit members, fails closed — **PASS**\n4. Repair: `D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR` recomputes the diff itself, rejects stale parent hash, hard-fails on any out-of-boundary pointer — **PASS**\n5. Persistence/resume: real `SqliteSaver`; `validate_resume_inputs` refuses on identity/frozen_digest/executable/evidence/accepted_bytes drift; resume refused outside `RESUMABLE_TERMINALS = {INTERRUPTED, PAUSED_PREREQUISITE}` — **PASS**\n6. Terminals: exactly the `RESUMABLE_TERMINALS`/`NON_RESUMABLE_TERMINALS` partition; terminal-write path exercised by the full, passing `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`/`test_plan26_workbook.py` suites — **PASS**\n7. CLI: one live dispatch (`_run_live`), fresh/resume both call `build_curriculum_factory_graph` once each; no simulation/session-bridge/Plan-25 reference reachable — **PASS**\n\n## 5. Adversarial/regression completeness, no waived tests (TEST item 5)\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.py` (26 tests, hash\n`0cbca18f412dd63b1c1a82fb535deb4ab50c8bcb8885fc02f2fa421d601c5a04`, matches\nreceipt, unchanged) maps every spec 17.2 adversarial row to a named test.\nThis audit reran the complete suite directly against current, final,\npost-rework code:\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime -rs\n```\n```\nSKIPPED [1] tests/runtime/test_plan26_lock_drift.py:220: pinned generator absent (needs pip==25.3, pip-tools==7.6.0); CI installs both\n1246 passed, 1 skipped, 406 subtests passed in 129.88s (0:02:09)\n```\n\nZero failures, zero errors, zero xfail/xpass. The one skip is an\nenvironment-only gap (a pinned pip/pip-tools generator not installed on this\nhost; the test's own reason string says CI installs both), not a test that\nwas deleted, weakened, or waived to hide a defect. Full output:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/full_suite_rerun.txt`.\n\n### Finding F1 — N40_CLI_CUTOVER evidence drift from re-running the required full suite (non-blocking, per patch P-N90-001, extended by direct verification)\n\n**rework_edges key:** `evidence_integrity_drift` · **owning node:** N40_CLI_CUTOVER (informational only; no rework routed)\n\nBefore this audit's own full-suite run, `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER`\nmatched its receipt exactly (digest\n`d495ab1b6f772cdd35aaadbe3e153b04790ebe89cc9b43e04125052d0091a493`, 0\nmismatches). Patch P-N90-001 pre-diagnosed that running the required full\nsuite (TEST item 5) necessarily rewrites `preflight_read_only.txt` with a\nnew `tempfile`-randomized path every time, via\n`test_preflight_read_only_evidence` — N40's own write set, structurally\nnon-reproducible regardless of any code change — and pre-authorized treating\nthat specific drift as non-blocking informational rather than routing it as\na `cli_or_cutover` finding.\n\nAfter this audit's own required suite run, this audit independently found a\n**second** file also drifted: `plan25_resume_refusal.txt`, beyond the\npatch's literal file list. Per the patch's own instruction, drift in \"a\ndifferent file\" was treated as a candidate genuine blocking finding pending\ninvestigation, not assumed exempt. Investigation\n(`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/evidence_drift_disposition.txt`) found:\n`test_plan25_root_refusal_evidence` (`tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py:745`)\nuses the identical mechanism as `test_preflight_read_only_evidence` — a\nfresh `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()` per invocation, whose path is embedded\nverbatim into the evidence text — and only that path substring differs\nbetween runs; exit code, error code, message shape, and file-tree assertions\nare byte-identical in structure. Both files live in\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py`, inside N40's own write set, and the\nprior N90 attempt's own Finding F1 (which P-N90-001 calls \"already-diagnosed\n... already precise and correct\") in fact named both files together as\nexhibiting this pattern. No other file in the evidence directory drifted; no\nother kind of difference and no evidence of behavioral regression was found\nin either file.\n\nDisposition: both `preflight_read_only.txt` and `plan25_resume_refusal.txt`\ndrift are the same structural, non-reproducible, pre-existing test artifact\n(a `tempfile`-randomized path embedded in a read-only CLI-probe evidence\ncapture) — recorded as non-blocking informational, not routed to N40 as a\n`cli_or_cutover` rework, consistent with and directly extending P-N90-001's\nreasoning to the second file this audit independently discovered.\n`import_audit.txt`, `cli_help.txt`, and `focused_test_run.txt` remain\nbyte-identical to their receipted content.\n\n## 6. Activation gate (TEST items 6-7)\n\n- N50 status: **PASSED** (original receipt, reconfirmed live in section 5).\n- N60 status: **NOT_AVAILABLE**. `results/N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF.result.v1.md`\n  shows Codex is live-authenticated (ChatGPT subscription) and both provider\n  hosts are network-reachable, but the Gemini CLI has no usable credential\n  in this environment (`gemini-api-key` auth mode selected,\n  `GEMINI_API_KEY`/`GOOGLE_API_KEY` unset, no Google account signed in) — a\n  real, non-simulated probe failure (exit 41), matching spec 6.3/7.3's hard\n  requirement for live Gemini execution on M05/M07 with no substitute\n  permitted. No partial transmission was attempted; no curriculum artifact\n  was produced or claimed. This is an external account/credential gap, not\n  an implementation defect — the runtime, transport, and preflight code all\n  report ready (`--preflight` returns `ready: true` for all 6 capabilities).\n- Therefore: N60 is `NOT_AVAILABLE` solely for a recorded external\n  prerequisite, and N50 passed. TEST item 7's condition for\n  `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` is met. TEST item 6's condition for\n  `ACTIVATED` (authorized live unit + full-release proof) is not met and was\n  not attempted, correctly.\n\n## Findings summary / rework_edges\n\n| Finding | rework_edges key | Owning node | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1: N40 evidence files (`preflight_read_only.txt`, `plan25_resume_refusal.txt`) drift on every full-suite run due to `tempfile`-randomized paths embedded by their own tests | `evidence_integrity_drift` | N40_CLI_CUTOVER | Non-blocking, informational, per patch P-N90-001 (extended by this audit's own investigation to the second file, found to be the identical mechanism) |\n| Receipt provenance ordering: N40/N50/N60 receipts predate later N20/N30/N31/N32 rework receipts | `receipt_cascade_invalidation` | harness (`prompt_graph_controller.py`), not a curriculum N-node | Non-blocking — N40/N50/N60 receipts never pinned the reworked files; this audit's own fresh full-suite rerun independently confirms the regression suite passes against current, final code |\n\nNeither finding blocks this verdict. Neither is a second or third occurrence\nof an unresolved ambiguous-ownership or missing-evidence finding.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nAll eight invariant classes pass on direct, current-code re-verification;\nthe complete regression/adversarial suite passes clean against the live,\nfinal (post-rework) code (1246 passed, 1 environment-only skip, 0 failures);\nthe production path is singular with no forbidden import or legacy\nfallback; every receipted artifact hash is verified current and valid, with\nthe one expected post-run evidence drift disposed of as non-blocking per\npatch P-N90-001 (extended to a second, structurally identical file this\naudit independently found). N60 correctly reports `NOT_AVAILABLE` for a\ngenuine, evidenced external prerequisite (live Gemini credential) rather\nthan any implementation gap. Per TEST item 7, the truthful verdict is:\n\n**`IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED`**\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":47,"newStart":1,"newLines":41,"lines":[" # N90_FINAL_AUDIT result"," ","+status: PASSED","+"," ## VERDICT: `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED`"," ","-This is an independent audit against the live top-level repository","-(`/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder`), not a trust of prior nodes'","-own claims: every receipt hash was recomputed, forbidden imports and the","-single-production-path claim were re-grepped against current code, seven core","-runtime invariants were re-derived from source by a fresh, independent","-read-only agent with no access to this conversation, and the complete","-`tests/runtime` suite was rerun end-to-end with the mandated interpreter","-(`/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python`).","+Independent audit against the live repository: every receipt hash was","+recomputed from scratch (not trusted from prior claims), the single-","+production-path and forbidden-import claims were re-grepped against current","+code, all eight invariant classes were re-derived from source, and the","+complete `tests/runtime` suite was rerun end-to-end with the mandated","+interpreter (`/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python`)."," "," ---"," "," ## 1. Spec-to-implementation traceability (TEST item 1)"," "," `contracts/traceability_matrix.v1.md` (sha256","-`edfc93d1bd412959133d523538150280785de8e9c3d4b0a4425b52e32fde2