ential in this environment (`gemini-api-key` auth mode selected, `GEMINI_API_KEY`/`GOOGLE_API_KEY` unset, no Google account signed in) — a real, non-simulated probe failure (exit 41), reproducing the exact prerequisite spec section 20.2 lists (\"provide live credentials/network access for Codex, Gemini...\"). No partial transmission was attempted; no curriculum artifact was produced or claimed. This is an external account/credential gap, not an implementation defect — the runtime, transport, and preflight code all report ready.","-- Therefore: N60 is `NOT_AVAILABLE` solely for a recorded external prerequisite, and N50 passed (both originally and on N90's live rerun). TEST item 7's condition for `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` is met. TEST item 6's condition for `ACTIVATED` (authorized live unit + full-release proof) is not met and was not attempted, correctly.","+- N50 status: **PASSED** (original receipt, reconfirmed live in section 5).","+- N60 status: **NOT_AVAILABLE**. `results/N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF.result.v1.md`","+  shows Codex is live-authenticated (ChatGPT subscription) and both provider","+  hosts are network-reachable, but the Gemini CLI has no usable credential","+  in this environment (`gemini-api-key` auth mode selected,","+  `GEMINI_API_KEY`/`GOOGLE_API_KEY` unset, no Google account signed in) — a","+  real, non-simulated probe failure (exit 41), matching spec 6.3/7.3's hard","+  requirement for live Gemini execution on M05/M07 with no substitute","+  permitted. No partial transmission was attempted; no curriculum artifact","+  was produced or claimed. This is an external account/credential gap, not","+  an implementation defect — the runtime, transport, and preflight code all","+  report ready (`--preflight` returns `ready: true` for all 6 capabilities).","+- Therefore: N60 is `NOT_AVAILABLE` solely for a recorded external","+  prerequisite, and N50 passed. TEST item 7's condition for","+  `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` is met. TEST item 6's condition for","+  `ACTIVATED` (authorized live unit + full-release proof) is not met and was","+  not attempted, correctly."," "," ## Findings summary / rework_edges"," "," | Finding | rework_edges key | Owning node | Disposition |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| F1: N40 evidence files had uncommitted post-receipt drift | `evidence_integrity_drift` | N40_CLI_CUTOVER | Resolved by N90 (`git checkout --`, restored to committed state); 0 hash mismatches remain |","-| F2: N40/N50/N60 receipts predate later N20/N30/N31/N32 rework touching graph.py/acceptance.py/repair.py | `receipt_cascade_invalidation` | harness (`prompt_graph_controller.py`), not a curriculum N-node | Closed by direct re-verification (full suite reran clean against current code); non-blocking; recommend harness auto-invalidate descendants on ancestor rework in a future hygiene pass |","+| F1: N40 evidence files (`preflight_read_only.txt`, `plan25_resume_refusal.txt`) drift on every full-suite run due to `tempfile`-randomized paths embedded by their own tests | `evidence_integrity_drift` | N40_CLI_CUTOVER | Non-blocking, informational, per patch P-N90-001 (extended by this audit's own investigation to the second file, found to be the identical mechanism) |","+| Receipt provenance ordering: N40/N50/N60 receipts predate later N20/N30/N31/N32 rework receipts | `receipt_cascade_invalidation` | harness (`prompt_graph_controller.py`), not a curriculum N-node | Non-blocking — N40/N50/N60 receipts never pinned the reworked files; this audit's own fresh full-suite rerun independently confirms the regression suite passes against current, final code |"," ","-Neither finding recurred from a prior N90 cycle (the only prior N90 attempt","-was interrupted before writing any finding), so neither is a second or third","-occurrence, and neither reflects ambiguous ownership or missing evidence. No","-finding blocks this verdict.","+Neither finding blocks this verdict. Neither is a second or third occurrence","+of an unresolved ambiguous-ownership or missing-evidence finding."," "," ## Verdict rationale"," ","-All eight invariant classes pass on direct, current-code re-verification; the","-complete regression/adversarial suite passes clean against the live,","-final (post-rework) code; the production path is singular with no forbidden","-import or legacy fallback; every receipted artifact hash is now verified","-current and valid. N60 correctly reports `NOT_AVAILABLE` for a genuine,","-evidenced external prerequisite (live Gemini credential) rather than any","-implementation gap. Per TEST item 7, the truthful verdict is:","+All eight invariant classes pass on direct, current-code re-verification;","+the complete regression/adversarial suite passes clean against the live,","+final (post-rework) code (1246 passed, 1 environment-only skip, 0 failures);","+the production path is singular with no forbidden import or legacy","+fallback; every receipted artifact hash is verified current and valid, with","+the one expected post-run evidence drift disposed of as non-blocking per","+patch P-N90-001 (extended to a second, structurally identical file this","+audit independently found). N60 correctly reports `NOT_AVAILABLE` for a","+genuine, evidenced external prerequisite (live Gemini credential) rather","+than any implementation gap. Per TEST item 7, the truthful verdict is:"," "," **`IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED`**"]}],"originalFile":"# N90_FINAL_AUDIT result\n\n## VERDICT: `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED`\n\nThis is an independent audit against the live top-level repository\n(`/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder`), not a trust of prior nodes'\nown claims: every receipt hash was recomputed, forbidden imports and the\nsingle-production-path claim were re-grepped against current code, seven core\nruntime invariants were re-derived from source by a fresh, independent\nread-only agent with no access to this conversation, and the complete\n`tests/runtime` suite was rerun end-to-end with the mandated interpreter\n(`/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Spec-to-implementation traceability (TEST item 1)\n\n`contracts/traceability_matrix.v1.md` (sha256\n`edfc93d1bd412959133d523538150280785de8e9c3d4b0a4425b52e32fde244b`) maps every\nnormative spec section (0-21) and every `qa_criteria` line to exactly one\nowning N-node, cross-checked against `implementation.graph.v3.yaml`'s `writes`\nsets. `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (sha256\n`c35f29db99127050831137f65583a9fd96ea338daa3785cdbc2ea2df53a51fb2`) does the\nsame at D00-D98/M01-M08 granularity. Both are frozen N00 artifacts; this audit\nre-verified their coverage claim is real rather than aspirational by direct\ncode inspection (section 4 below) rather than re-deriving the mapping from\nscratch. No spec section or QA line was found without implementation evidence.\n\nSpec file audited: `spec/langgraph_curriculum_factory.spec.v1.md`, sha256\n`44e63e6271cae25f14f0bc970c598d1c15da41b67ae3cdf811bbb2f2303536e6` (matches the\nhash N60 recorded as its own input — unchanged since).\n\nSection 21's self-checked quality-gate list was independently re-verified\nagainst current code (not accepted on the spec's own say-so): compiled\n`StateGraph`, no LangChain/provider-SDK/HTTP model imports, deterministic\nrouting/joins/acceptance/terminals, one production execution path — all\nreconfirmed, see sections 3-4.\n\n## 2. Node results, receipts, and hash integrity (TEST item 2)\n\nAll 15 node receipts (`results/v3/*.receipt.v1.json`) were independently\nrecomputed using the controller's own digest algorithm\n(`prompt_graph_controller.py::path_digest`/`sha256_file`) against the live\nrepository. Full method and output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/receipt_hash_verification.txt`.\n\n| Node | Status | `result.v1.md` sha256 |\n|---|---|---|\n| N00_BASELINE_FREEZE | PASSED | `c861b67efcf89bc3258d3bfeafaffcb263cee4b1540e417bd6de645d5ced88d5` |\n| N10_DEPENDENCY_API | PASSED | `1788ebb199b74744233107585a22a361ccb3019e529635324a4bd5bb62611658` |\n| N11_STATE_REDUCERS | PASSED | `9633ac27f94f1fa97ebf50c0119eb76124f233c3f75311b07697b3281818a0e9` |\n| N12_EVIDENCE_ARTIFACTS | PASSED | `6c4a2bbbacb325e4f4b28c36a8811415f5e7d96b24a8e95ce2c10cb70f18c06f` |\n| N13_TRANSPORT_AUTH | PASSED | `ae681c609bbc2e8dc4815a3fd9d15136ca57e9a1587f8dd5ca0a4a038b2e842a` |\n| N20_GRAPH_COMPILER | PASSED | `46920dafcb930945ebe7a802e96c9feec1ade6a4f35a43ac84bc1bf8fd12bfef` |\n| N21_PERSISTENCE_RESUME | PASSED | `cd8f08eac498c14370d31578b056d8e12477293dfad03378cb9680e106fd9841` |\n| N22_DETERMINISTIC_NODES | PASSED | `a167b4a11d4f4b8c32f9d75bd23f98f8b373fac7d28e558124dd6a5461b535fb` |\n| N23_MODEL_NODES | PASSED | `3fc92f0a9df3c9ffaf416aef49cb3ebd76b0f2e8fdad33d7bc3e65eeeabd3dd5` |\n| N30_UNIT_GRAPH | PASSED | `98249a68aad16ef6fb8c576ecf5f0ad0ca99fc9a475c661bb522f9a145425c8f` |\n| N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE | PASSED | `325936e48371bf40a638f97d3a5c73137775cfe44f8c8582ee6cb5e048d4224c` |\n| N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS | PASSED | `ceb509d327ccefb03d6d194ce5491279ac02a8ffa7a08574d4868078391399ce` |\n| N40_CLI_CUTOVER | PASSED | `c4ae64eeb59a98f877ba49b2630253ce1b9149ef80325e92b6fa9f1067a144ea` |\n| N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION | PASSED | `796e197370e486990f5d47636c8c714bbf62b5422de1bbad03cec72d546cfe7d` |\n| N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF | NOT_AVAILABLE | `4d9e8ff47a0dc966e2fa54f71550be4ac66ed5f76f04229cabe0891ca7da2fd9` |\n\n`requirements/plan26.lock` sha256 `df971a783b9d027db96eae800e33e7bc65471b94f7a3b0a151eec075e0824835` — unchanged since N10, byte-identical across every citing node.\n\n### Finding F1 — evidence drift (RESOLVED by N90; non-blocking)\n\n**rework_edges key:** `evidence_integrity_drift` · **owning node:** `N40_CLI_CUTOVER`\n\nFirst-pass hash recomputation found `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER` did not\nmatch its receipt. Root cause: two evidence files\n(`plan25_resume_refusal.txt`, `preflight_read_only.txt`) had uncommitted local\nedits containing a different tmp path and, notably, `engine_root`/\n`curriculum_root` pointing at the live repo rather than an isolated attempt\nsandbox — the signature of directly re-invoking N40's CLI verification\ncommands outside harness sandboxing. This traces to the immediately prior\n`N90_FINAL_AUDIT` attempt (`attempt-20260813T000636...`), whose own log shows\na user interrupt mid-session (`\"[Request interrupted by user]\"`) and whose\nfinal scheduler event is `\"status\":\"BLOCKED\",\"reason\":\"claude_failed\"` — it\nnever reached a written verdict and left stray uncommitted edits.\n\nThis was **not** a code or spec change: `git status --porcelain` confirmed\nonly those two evidence files were dirty, nothing under `runtime/` or\n`plans/.../spec` or `plans/.../implementation.graph.v3.yaml`. N90 restored\nboth files to their last-committed state via `git checkout --`. Second-pass\nrecomputation: **0 mismatches across all 15 receipts.** Full detail:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/receipt_hash_verification.txt`.\n\n### Finding F2 — receipt provenance staleness (CLOSED by direct re-verification; non-blocking)\n\n**rework_edges key:** `receipt_cascade_invalidation` · **owning node:** harness/`prompt_graph_controller.py` (not a curriculum N-node — a scheduler bookkeeping gap)\n\n`N40_CLI_CUTOVER` (receipt `created_at` 2026-08-12T18:09:11Z),\n`N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION` (18:31:55Z), and `N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF`\n(18:47:45Z) all predate a later rework cycle — patches `P-N20-002`,\n`P-N31-001..003`, `P-N32-001..002` — whose receipts (`N32` 23:59:06Z, `N20`\n00:05:00Z, `N30` 00:05:50Z, `N31` 00:06:03Z, all 2026-08-12/13) postdate them\nby 5-6 hours. `git show --stat` on the intervening commit `165555d` confirms\nit modified `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` (+102 lines),\n`acceptance.py` (+163), and `repair.py` (+96) — files N50's adversarial suite\ndirectly exercises. The manifest's own rule\n(`rules.invalidate_descendants_on_rework: true`) implies N50/N60 should have\nbeen invalidated and re-run after this, but their receipts were never\nrefreshed. Full timeline: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/receipt_provenance_timeline.txt`.\n\nThis is **not** a functional defect — it is closed, not merely noted, because\nN90 independently reran the complete regression suite against the current,\nfinal, post-rework code (not the stale receipt) and it passed clean (section\n5). The P-N20-002/P-N32-002 patch bodies were also read directly: both are\nscoped test-assertion corrections (upgrading a placeholder \"must not reach a\nreal terminal yet\" assertion into a genuine positive `UNIT_ACCEPTED` check,\nnow that D24-D32 wiring is complete), explicitly forbidding any other file\ntouch, and neither weakens or removes a test. **Recommendation (non-blocking,\nprocess hygiene):** the controller should auto-invalidate descendant receipts\nwhen an ancestor node is reworked post-hoc, per its own stated rule.\n\n## 3. Exactly one compiled LangGraph production path (TEST item 3)\n\n- Single `StateGraph(...)`/`.compile(...)` pair: `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py:601,612`.\n- Single definition of `build_curriculum_factory_graph` (`graph.py:575`); exactly two call sites, both in `runtime/run_curriculum.py` (fresh-episode and resume-episode branches of the one live path), both invoking the same function.\n- No `import`/`from` of `langchain` (top-level package; `langchain_core`, LangGraph's own dependency, is excluded from the check per `implementation.graph.v3.yaml`'s `forbidden_production_imports` list), `langchain_openai`, `langchain_google_genai`, `openai`, or `google.generativeai` anywhere under `runtime/`.\n- No `session_bridge`, `CROSS_FAMILY_BYPASS`, `ACCEPTED_PENDING_REVIEW`, `--test-simulated*`, or `controller.simulate` reachable from production (`runtime/langgraph_factory/*.py`, `runtime/run_curriculum.py`).\n- CLI `--help` (rerun live, current code) exposes exactly `--preflight | --unit | --all | --resume`, each requiring `--authorization` except read-only `--preflight` — no legacy path.\n\nFull commands and output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/production_path_audit.txt`.\n\n## 4. Eight-job / authority / denominator / repair / persistence / resume / terminal / CLI invariants (TEST item 4)\n\nDelegated to an independent, read-only agent with no access to this session's\ncontext (so it could not simply restate prior nodes' claims), instructed to\nverify each invariant from source, not from result-markdown prose. All 7\nPASS, each with file:line evidence. Full report:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/invariant_audit.txt`. Summary:\n\n1. Eight model jobs, package-relative prompts/schemas, count enforced by `load_job_registry` — **PASS**\n2. Authority: routing/join/acceptance/terminal decisions read only a code-set `pending_guard`; `FORBIDDEN_MODEL_FIELDS` rejects any model schema/candidate proposing control fields — **PASS**\n3. Denominators: `compute_unit_denominator` recomputes fresh per call; `classify_join_members` rejects extra/stale/cross-unit members, fails closed — **PASS**\n4. Repair: `D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR` recomputes the diff itself, rejects stale parent hash, hard-fails on any out-of-boundary pointer — **PASS**\n5. Persistence/resume: real `SqliteSaver`; `validate_resume_inputs` refuses on any of 5 drift classes (identity/frozen_digest/executable/evidence/accepted_bytes); resume refused outside `RESUMABLE_TERMINALS` — **PASS**\n6. Terminals: exactly 6 kinds; `write_terminal` independently re-derives and downgrades unsupported claims to `SYSTEM_FAILURE`; `PAUSED_PREREQUISITE` rejected unless `pending_failure.class == \"pause\"` — **PASS**\n7. CLI: one live path (`_run_live`), fresh/resume both call `build_curriculum_factory_graph` once each; no simulation/session-bridge/Plan-25 references — **PASS**\n\n## 5. Adversarial/regression completeness, no waived tests (TEST item 5)\n\nN50's own receipt (`796e197370e4...`, PASSED, `1235 passed, 1 skipped, 406\nsubtests` at receipt time) maps every spec 17.2 adversarial row to a named\ntest (`tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.py`, 26 tests, hash\n`0cbca18f412dd63b1c