al transmission was attempted; no curriculum artifact was produced or claimed. This is an external account/credential gap, not an implementation defect — the runtime, transport, and preflight code all report ready.\n- Therefore: N60 is `NOT_AVAILABLE` solely for a recorded external prerequisite, and N50 passed (both originally and on N90's live rerun). TEST item 7's condition for `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` is met. TEST item 6's condition for `ACTIVATED` (authorized live unit + full-release proof) is not met and was not attempted, correctly.\n\n## Findings summary / rework_edges\n\n| Finding | rework_edges key | Owning node | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1: N40 evidence files had uncommitted post-receipt drift | `evidence_integrity_drift` | N40_CLI_CUTOVER | Resolved by N90 (`git checkout --`, restored to committed state); 0 hash mismatches remain |\n| F2: N40/N50/N60 receipts predate later N20/N30/N31/N32 rework touching graph.py/acceptance.py/repair.py | `receipt_cascade_invalidation` | harness (`prompt_graph_controller.py`), not a curriculum N-node | Closed by direct re-verification (full suite reran clean against current code); non-blocking; recommend harness auto-invalidate descendants on ancestor rework in a future hygiene pass |\n\nNeither finding recurred from a prior N90 cycle (the only prior N90 attempt\nwas interrupted before writing any finding), so neither is a second or third\noccurrence, and neither reflects ambiguous ownership or missing evidence. No\nfinding blocks this verdict.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nAll eight invariant classes pass on direct, current-code re-verification; the\ncomplete regression/adversarial suite passes clean against the live,\nfinal (post-rework) code; the production path is singular with no forbidden\nimport or legacy fallback; every receipted artifact hash is now verified\ncurrent and valid. N60 correctly reports `NOT_AVAILABLE` for a genuine,\nevidenced external prerequisite (live Gemini credential) rather than an